cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "InvaRadar: early detection of invasive plants from satellite embeddings, drones and citizen photos"
message: "If you use this software or its maps, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Konkov
    given-names: Dmitrij V.
    alias: KonkovDV
version: 1.2.0
date-released: 2026-10-30
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - invasive species
  - Heracleum sosnowskyi
  - Solidago
  - remote sensing
  - AlphaEarth Foundations
  - species distribution model
  - Rust
abstract: >-
  InvaRadar maps Heracleum sosnowskyi and Solidago spp. at 10 m over a 4,225 km² window
  covering Moscow and the inner belt of Moscow Oblast from AlphaEarth Foundations
  satellite embeddings, landscape context, spread corridors and terrain (Priority-Flood, D8, TWI, HAND), validated
  with 5 km spatial blocks and a forward-in-time test. Hotspots are ranked by risk to people and receive treatment
  prescriptions that follow the Water Code of the Russian Federation and sanitary rules. A Rust core computes
  features, wall-to-wall inference, hotspots, routes and stratified validation samples.
